From f1aa938abf956aae93abb770e0b7fa912197a7cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 14:53:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Preselect GBA vs GBA, label and fully hide portrait-less
 models

Three fixes from 1.4.1 field testing, shipped together as v1.4.2:

- One-tap Orre Colosseum now pins the VS mode row to GBA vs GBA instead
  of holding it on GC vs GBA. The layout global doubles as the mode row
  (0 = GC vs GBA, 1 = GBA vs GBA, >= 2 = tag), so the old pin of 0 both
  showed the wrong mode and reverted every attempt to change it. Value 1
  is verified against the layout table (ports {2,3}, matching this
  fork's SI config) and skips the GC-pad presence gates.

- The bust hide now also zeroes the class-0 widget pair (0x201/0x208).
  That column is every bust descriptor's compile-time default record, so
  screens that draw before the per-class re-crop -- the team preview
  screen -- still showed the GC protagonist for portrait-less picks. A
  whole-image scan confirmed the fourteen records are the only path to
  the bust atlas, so this closes the last surface. Emitted only while a
  hide is active, so genuine GC-vs-GBA sessions are untouched.

- Model pickers on all surfaces now label the sixty models without
  pre-battle art as "(no portrait)" (with an explanatory note) instead
  of a tier marking, so it is visible up front that only the six GBA
  protagonists have the full presentation.
